From: Peter Strand <peter@zarquon.se>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] soc: apple: sep: instrument boot, and probe the ROM for liveness

On a j413 (M2 Air) with the sep node enabled, apple_sep binds cleanly — probe()
completes, so the sepfw region resolved, both manifests parsed, the mailbox was
acquired and MSG_BOOT_TZ0 was sent — but 25e408000.mbox-recv stays at zero
interrupts forever. The SEP never acks. The stub driver cannot tell us why,
because it logs nothing and drops every message it does not recognise.

Two changes:

1. Log every inbound message before dispatch, un-comment the endpoint
   advertisement handler, and report each boot-handshake ack. Nothing is
   silently discarded any more.

2. Probe the boot ROM with GETRAND before attempting the boot handshake. This
   is the exact message m1n1's sep_get_random() uses (EP 0xFF, type 16, reply
   type 116), and EP_BOOT is that same 0xFF ROM endpoint. It discriminates the
   two candidate explanations for the silence:

     GETRAND replies  -> ROM is alive and listening; TZ0 is being refused or
                         ignored for some other reason.
     GETRAND silent   -> the ROM endpoint is gone, i.e. SEPOS was already
                         booted by iBoot, and this driver's TZ0/IMG4 path
                         cannot work on a machine booted this way.

Diagnostic only — no functional change to the boot sequence beyond one extra
message sent ahead of it.

Apply against AsahiLinux/linux, branch `asahi`.
